WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.007
Method chaining is a way to connect several DataFrame operations into one readable sequence.

00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:08.717
Look at the code from top to bottom.

00:00:08.717 --> 00:00:11.387
We start with the orders DataFrame.

00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:17.722
Then we use query to keep only orders with an amount of at least seventy.

00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:25.812
After that, assign creates a new fee column, and sort values arranges the remaining rows from the largest amount to the

00:00:25.812 --> 00:00:32.387
smallest. Before you run the code, try to predict which orders will remain and which one will appear first.

00:00:32.865 --> 00:00:41.794
When you are writing a chain, placing each method on a separate line inside parentheses makes the logic much easier to

00:00:41.794 --> 00:00:48.449
follow. It also makes debugging easier because you can identify the step that may be causing a problem.

00:00:48.449 --> 00:00:52.264
Run the code in the browser and inspect the output.

00:00:52.264 --> 00:00:57.804
Then change the threshold from seventy to fifty and run it again.

00:00:57.804 --> 00:01:04.156
Notice how one small change near the beginning of the workflow changes everything that follows.
